blocks.en:
Automatic Validation. Before an example is admitted to the frozen benchmark, it passes a sequence of
automatic consistency checks covering the main construction joins. These checks verify that:
(i) the question and reference answer correspond to the same verified
world-state fact;
(ii) all required evidence units are represented in the question-specific
annotation;
(iii) grounding targets resolve to valid admitted observations;
(iv) strong configurations contain support for every mandatory evidence unit;
(v) weak configurations remove support for at least one mandatory unit;
(vi) the strong and weak examples preserve the same underlying question and
semantic fact; and
(vii) no configuration is admitted with unresolved structural or grounding
inconsistencies. The audit is deliberately conservative. Failed joins, invalid
grounding, or internally inconsistent support records are repaired when the
underlying evidence can be verified; otherwise, the affected pair is
rejected.

